Description: Run the tests which use the CLIPBOARD selection with no other test at the same time.
 All tests run on the one X display xvfb-run starts for them, and both clipboard and textbuffer copy and paste through
 its CLIPBOARD selection. When one of them claims the selection while the other is between a copy and a paste, that
 paste goes through the X server and has not arrived when the test checks the text, so textbuffer fails with, for
 example, ("defabc" == "abcdefabc"). Next to clipboard running in a loop, textbuffer failed 5 of 300 runs this way,
 and alone none of 300.
Author: Mitar <mitar.git@tnode.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-05
--- a/testsuite/gtk/meson.build
+++ b/testsuite/gtk/meson.build
@@ -56,6 +56,14 @@
 xfail = [
 ]
 
+# Tests which copy and paste through the CLIPBOARD selection of the display, which all tests share. A test which
+# claims the selection while another is between its copy and its paste makes that paste go through the X server, so
+# it has not arrived when the test checks the text. They run with no other test at the same time.
+clipboard_tests = [
+  'clipboard',
+  'textbuffer',
+]
+
 is_debug = get_option('buildtype').startswith('debug')
 
 test_cargs = []
@@ -108,6 +116,7 @@
               'GTK_TEST_MESON=1',
             ],
        suite: suites,
+       is_parallel: not clipboard_tests.contains(test_name),
   )
 endforeach
 
